.TH ZERODDS-OPCUA-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-opcua-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-opcua-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/opcua-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing the OMG DDS-OPCUA Gateway 1.0 daemon's
.IR opc.tcp " server, client and Part-14 PubSub connections."
The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-opcua-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.IR crates/opcua-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::from_config .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " opcua ", " acl ", " metrics .
.PP
An unknown key
.I inside
a known section (e.g. an unrecognized
.BR opcua.server. \fIkey\fR )
stops the start with the file and line named; an unrecognized top-level key
is a WARN line on stderr and otherwise ignored \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed, so
keys and passwords belong in the environment, not in the file.
.PP
The sections of
.BR opcua :
.BR idl ", " gateway_config ", " server ", " client ", " pubsub .
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS opcua
.TP
.B idl
List of
.I .idl
file paths, compiled at startup. Every
.B dds_type
named anywhere below must be declared in one of them.
.TP
.B gateway_config
Path to an OMG DDS-OPCUA Gateway 1.0 \(sc10 XML file: one or more
.IR <bridge> " elements, each with a " domain_id
and any number of
.IR <dds_to_ua_connection> " / " <ua_to_dds_connection> " entries "
(\c
.IR dds_topic ", " dds_type ", optional " browse_path " / " node_id \c
). A
.I node_id
replaces the connection's sample root's identity (a collision with an
existing node refuses the start); a
.I browse_path
adds an additional
.I Organizes
reference chain from the well-known
.I Objects
folder (ns0;i=85) to the same root \(em both additive to the default
.I Topic:<name>
reachability, never a replacement of it (\(sc5.2 of the spec file).
.SS opcua.server
.TP
.B enabled
Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B bind
.I opc.tcp
bind address. Default
.IR 0.0.0.0:4840 .
.TP
.B security_policies
List of
.IR none ", " basic256sha256 ", " aes128_sha256_rsaoaep ", " aes256_sha256_rsapss .
Any entry other than
.I none
requires
.B certificate_der
and
.BR private_key_pem ,
and the build feature
.IR crypto ;
the start refuses otherwise.
.TP
.B certificate_der
This server's own DER certificate, sent on the wire as-is.
.TP
.B private_key_pem
This server's RSA private key, PKCS#8 PEM.
.TP
.B trusted_client_certificate_der
The one trusted client's DER certificate.
.TP
.B trusted_client_public_key_pem
The one trusted client's RSA public key,
.I SubjectPublicKeyInfo
PEM \(em a separate file from the certificate above; this daemon has no
X.509 parser to split one certificate into both (\(sc7.1 of the spec file).
.TP
.B security_groups
The SecurityGroups whose keys this daemon makes and hands out as a
Security Key Service (Part 14 \(sc8; build features
.IR crypto " and " pubsub-security ).
Each entry:
.B security_group_id
(unique),
.B policy
(\c
.IR aes128-ctr " | " aes256-ctr " | " aes256-gcm ),
.B key_lifetime_ms
(default 3600000),
.B max_future_key_count
(default 3),
.B max_past_key_count
(default 1),
.B key_subjects
(the users that may get the keys with
.IR GetSecurityKeys ,
over an encrypted channel) and
.B admin_subjects
(the users that may call
.IR InvalidateKeys " and " ForceKeyRotation ,
over a signed channel).
.TP
.B roles
The users of the well-known roles of a Security Key Service (Part 14
\(sc8.8; build features
.IR crypto " and " pubsub-security ),
each a list of user names:
.B security_key_server_admin
(may add and remove SecurityGroups and their folders with
.IR AddSecurityGroup ", " RemoveSecurityGroup ", " AddSecurityGroupFolder " and " RemoveSecurityGroupFolder ,
and invalidate or rotate the keys of every group; with a user here the
daemon is a Security Key Service even without
.BR security_groups ),
.B security_key_server_access
(may get the keys of every group) and
.B security_key_server_push
(may push keys with
.I SetSecurityKeys
for every connection with
.BR "key_source: push" ).
.TP
.B historical
Section with one key,
.BR topics :
a list of Historical Access entries (Spec \(sc9.3.4.4). Each entry:
.B dds_topic
(must match a
.I dds_to_ua_connection
topic \(em a name matching none, or matching only a
.IR ua_to_dds_connection ", is a load-time error)"
and
.B depth
(the per-leaf retention bound, an integer of at least 1). Every leaf of the
named topic is marked historizing (\c
.IR Historizing " = " true ", the " HistoryRead " " AccessLevel
bit set) and answers the
.I HistoryRead
service (Part 4 \(sc5.10.3).
.SS opcua.client
.TP
.B enabled
Default
.IR false .
.TP
.B servers
List of foreign OPC-UA servers to browse/subscribe as a client. Each entry:
.RS
.TP
.B endpoint_url
e.g.
.IR opc.tcp://plc.local:4840 .
.TP
.B nodes
List of entries with
.B node_id
(canonical
.IR ns=N;i=NNN " or " ns=N;s=NAME " form; " g= " / " b=
are not supported),
.BR dds_topic ,
.B dds_type
(default: the value of
.BR dds_topic ),
.B field_path
(default: empty \(em the whole, scalar sample) and
.B keyed
(default false).
.RE
.SS opcua.pubsub
.TP
.B enabled
Default
.IR false .
.TP
.B connections
List of Part-14 UADP connections. Each entry:
.RS
.TP
.B name
Free-form label.
.TP
.B local_addr
UDP bind address. Default
.IR 0.0.0.0:0 .
.TP
.B multicast_addr
UADP multicast group + port, e.g.
.IR 224.0.0.22:4840 .
.TP
.B publisher_id
Numeric PublisherId. Default
.IR 1 .
.TP
.B publishers
DDS \(-> UADP entries:
.BR dds_topic ", " dds_type ", " keyed ", " writer_group_id ", " dataset_writer_id ,
.B dataset_name
(default: the value of
.BR dds_topic )
and
.B publish_interval_ms
(default 1000).
.TP
.B subscribers
UADP \(-> DDS entries:
.BR dds_topic ", " dds_type ", " keyed ,
.B dataset_name
(default: the value of
.BR dds_topic )
and
.B fields
(required \(em the remote Publisher's own field order).
.TP
.B security
Part 14 \(sc8 UADP message security (build feature
.BR pubsub-security ).
Omit entirely for cleartext UADP. Fields:
.B policy
(\c
.IR aes128-ctr " | " aes256-ctr " | " aes256-gcm ),
.B security_group_id
and
.B key_source
(\c
.IR static " (default) | " local " | " sks " | " push ),
where the keys come from (Part 14 \(sc5.4.5):
.RS
.TP
.I static
One key that does not rotate:
.B token_id
(default 1) and
.BR signing_key ", " encrypting_key ", " key_nonce
(hex-encoded;
.B signing_key
empty for
.IR aes256-gcm ,
whose integrity comes from the GCM tag). A hex-decoded key whose length
disagrees with its policy is refused at load time.
.TP
.I local
The keys of this daemon's own SecurityGroup of
.B security_group_id
(see
.BR opcua.server.security_groups ).
.TP
.I sks
Pulled with
.I GetSecurityKeys
from the Security Key Service in
.BR sks :
.BR endpoint_url ,
.B channel_policy
(\c
.IR basic256sha256 " (default) | " aes128_sha256_rsaoaep " | " aes256_sha256_rsapss ;
the call is made over a SecureChannel that encrypts),
.BR certificate_der ", " private_key_pem
(this daemon's),
.BR server_certificate_der ", " server_public_key_pem
(the SKS's),
.BR username ", " password ", " user_token_policy_id
(default
.IR user )
and
.B requested_key_count
(default 3). The keys are pulled again at half their lifetime and when a
message names a token there is no key for; they rotate as the SKS says.
.TP
.I push
Pushed with
.I SetSecurityKeys
by the session of
.B push_subject
over an encrypted channel.
.PP
Until the first keys are there, the connection publishes and reads
nothing.
.RE
.RE
.SS acl
.TP
.B default_deny
Default
.IR false .
With rules present, a topic no rule names for the operation asked is
denied when
.B default_deny
is true, allowed when false.
.TP
.B rules
List of entries with
.BR subject ,
.B allow_read
(list of DDS topic names) and
.BR allow_write .
Two layers are enforced: topic exposure at start time (a topic no rule
names is not materialized/registered at all, for any client, when any
rule exists or
.B default_deny
is true) and, for a Write against this daemon's own server, the
.B subject
dimension per OPC-UA session (via
.IR Server::set_write_hook ;
\(sc6.2/\(sc7.2 of the spec file). A denied Write is
.I Bad_UserAccessDenied
before the AddressSpace is touched.
.TP
.B allow_anonymous
Default
.IR true .
Whether the
.I UserStore
accepts the Anonymous
.IR UserIdentityToken .
.TP
.B users
List of UserName credentials this daemon's server accepts at
ActivateSession:
.BR username ", " password ", " policy_id
(default
.IR user ).
A user's own
.B username
is the
.I subject
string
.B rules
match against \(em without a named user, every session is Anonymous and
.B rules
has nothing to differ on.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Default
.IR false .
.TP
.B listen
Bind address for
.IR GET " " /metrics .
Default
.I 127.0.0.1:9095
when
.B enabled
and this is empty.
.TP
.B otlp_endpoint
An OTel collector's OTLP/HTTP base URL, e.g.
.IR http://127.0.0.1:4318 .
Omit to export no spans. Exports one coarse-grained
.I zerodds-opcua-bridged.opc_tcp.accept
span per accepted
.I opc.tcp
connection, every 5 seconds and once more on shutdown.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.I packaging/linux/configs/opcua-bridged.yaml.example
for a complete, commented file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-opcua-bridged (1).
